{"id":"chatcmpl-33af3601-bc4f-4151-aa19-f25fa772ec8a","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250542,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-tool verification strategy for spatial laterality determination in medical imaging. The key insight is using anatomical landmarks (anterior/posterior course relative to sternum/spine) on a lateral view to infer laterality, rather than relying on direct left/right labeling. Cross-validation with independent models and targeted ROI zooming reinforce confidence before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When laterality is ambiguous on a primary view, use an orthogonal view and infer side from anatomical landmark relationships (e.g., anterior course near sternum implies right-sided SVC entry).\",\n    \"Cross-validate a critical visual finding with at least two independent tools/models before finalizing, especially when the finding is subtle or small.\",\n    \"Use targeted ROI cropping/zooming on the region of interest to visually confirm presence and course of small linear structures before answering.\",\n    \"Re-query the expert tool with progressively more specific questions (presence -> course -> laterality) to decompose a compound spatial judgment into verifiable steps.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Decompose spatial/laterality questions into landmark-relative descriptions; use orthogonal views and zoomed ROIs to confirm subtle structures.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification\": \"Chain independent tools for the same sub-question; treat agreement as confidence and disagreement as a signal to re-query with sharper, more specific prompts.\",\n    \"Ambiguous binary choice tasks\": \"Convert the binary choice into a physical/geometric discriminator (anterior vs posterior, proximal vs distal) that maps deterministically to the answer options.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding is present on at least two independent tools/views before deciding laterality.\",\n    \"Verify the anatomical landmark reasoning explicitly maps to the chosen option (e.g., anterior course -> right-sided entry -> option B).\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":660,"total_tokens":1061,"completion_tokens":401,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":660},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":401}}}